/-!
# Hypothesis (3) of Stacks 02S6 at the embedded points does not suffice

The third hypothesis of Stacks 02S6 is a condition on the associated points of the coherent
sheaf `F` on `X ×_S 𝐏¹_S`: "for any associated point `ξ` of `F` either
`ξ ∉ (X × 0) ∪ (X × ∞)` or `δ(ξ) < k`". A variant of the text (the one in the audit extraction of
the tag) restricts it to the *embedded* associated points. Read that way the lemma is false, and
this file is the refutation.

The instance is the one the module documentation of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Chow/FibreCycles/CoherentFibreComparison.lean` describes. Take the
Chow situation over a field, `Stacks.Chow.fieldChowSituation K`, with `X = S = Spec K`, `f = 𝟙`,
`k = 0`, and for `F` the coherent sheaf carried by the image of the zero section of
`𝐏¹_K ⟶ Spec K`, that is the direct image `Stacks.Chow.fieldZeroSectionSheaf K` of the structure
sheaf of `Spec K` along that section. Then

* `Supp(F)` is the image of the zero section, every point of which has relative dimension `0`
  along the structure morphism of the family, so hypothesis (1) holds with room to spare;
* `F_∞ = 0` and `Supp(F₀) ⊆ Spec K`, whose delta-dimension is `0`, so hypothesis (2) holds;
* `Supp(F)` is a single point, so `F` has no two distinct associated points and hence no
  embedded associated point at all: hypothesis (3) holds vacuously.

All three hypotheses therefore hold. But `[F₀]₀` has a strictly positive coefficient at the
unique point of `Spec K`, while `[F_∞]₀ = 0`, and on `Spec K` no nonzero `0`-cycle is rationally
equivalent to zero: rational equivalence of `0`-cycles is generated by principal divisors on
integral closed subschemes of `δ`-dimension `1`, and every closed subscheme of `Spec K` has
`δ`-dimension `0`. So the conclusion fails.

The condition at every *associated* point of `F`, which is hypothesis (3) of
`Stacks.Chow.rationallyEquivalent_cycleAssociatedToCoherentSheaf_fibres`, is what the instance
fails: the unique associated point of `F` lies on the zero section and has relative dimension
`k`. So the registered form of the tag is untouched by the counterexample. Stacks' own proof of
02S6 reads hypothesis (3) off as "`ξ` is not an associated point of `F`", so nothing in the
source depends on the weaker reading.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Chow.nontrivial_quotSMulTop_iff` — for a finite module over a local ring and a
  parameter in the maximal ideal, the quotient by that parameter is nonzero exactly when the
  module is. This is Nakayama's lemma in the form the support computation needs.
* `Stacks.Chow.mem_supp_pullback_iff_of_exists_span_eq_ker` — the support of the pullback of a
  sheaf of finite type along a locally principal preimmersion is the preimage of the support.
* `Stacks.Chow.eq_zero_of_isRationallyEquivalentToZero_fieldChowSituation` (in
  `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Chow.FibreCycles.EmbeddedPointCounterexample`) — on `Spec K` the
  only `0`-cycle rationally equivalent to zero is the zero cycle. This is where the conclusion of
  Stacks 02S6 fails.
* `Stacks.Chow.fieldZeroSectionSheaf` — the coherent sheaf of the counterexample.
* `Stacks.Chow.not_isEmbeddedAssociatedPoint_fieldZeroSectionSheaf` — it has no embedded
  associated point, so hypothesis (3) is vacuous for it.
* `Stacks.Chow.not_forall_rationallyEquivalent_of_isEmbeddedAssociatedPoint` — **the
  refutation**: there is no implication from hypotheses (1), (2) and (3) of Stacks 02S6, with (3)
  read at the embedded associated points, to its conclusion.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 02S6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02S6)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 05AK](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05AK)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02RW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02RW)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 00DV](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00DV)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits TopologicalSpace

universe u

namespace Stacks.Chow

/-! ### Nakayama's lemma for a single parameter -/

/-- **Nakayama's lemma, for one parameter in the maximal ideal.** For a finite module `M` over a
local ring `A` and `t ∈ 𝔪_A`, the quotient `M / tM` is nonzero exactly when `M` is: one direction
is that a quotient of a zero module is zero, and the other is Stacks 00DV (2) applied to the
ideal `(t)`, which lies in the Jacobson radical. -/
@[ega "IV 2.5.5.4" "special case"]
theorem nontrivial_quotSMulTop_iff {A M : Type*} [CommRing A] [IsLocalRing A] [AddCommGroup M]
    [Module A M] [Module.Finite A M] {t : A} (ht : t ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) :
    Nontrivial (QuotSMulTop t M) ↔ Nontrivial M := by
  rw [Submodule.Quotient.nontrivial_iff]
  refine ⟨fun h => ?_, fun hM htop => ?_⟩
  · rw [← not_subsingleton_iff_nontrivial]
    intro hs
    have : Subsingleton (Submodule A M) := (Submodule.subsingleton_iff A).mpr hs
    exact h (Subsingleton.elim _ _)
  · have hle : (⊤ : Submodule A M) ≤ (Ideal.span {t}) • (⊤ : Submodule A M) := by
      rw [Submodule.ideal_span_singleton_smul]
      exact htop.ge
    have hbot : (⊤ : Submodule A M) = ⊥ :=
      Submodule.eq_bot_of_le_smul_of_le_jacobson_bot (Ideal.span {t}) ⊤ Module.Finite.fg_top hle
        ((Ideal.span_le.mpr (Set.singleton_subset_iff.mpr ht)).trans
          (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal_le_jacobson ⊥))
    obtain ⟨a, b, hab⟩ := hM
    rw [Submodule.eq_bot_iff] at hbot
    exact hab ((hbot a Submodule.mem_top).trans (hbot b Submodule.mem_top).symm)

/-! ### The support of a pullback along a locally principal preimmersion -/

/-- **The support of a pullback is the preimage of the support**, at a point where the kernel of
the stalk map is principal and for a sheaf of finite type. The stalk of the pullback has the
length of `M / tM` for `M` the stalk of the sheaf and `t` a generator of that kernel, by
`Stacks.Chow.length_stalk_pullback_eq_length_quotSMulTop`, and `M / tM` is nonzero exactly when
`M` is, by `Stacks.Chow.nontrivial_quotSMulTop_iff`; the generator lies in the maximal ideal
because it is killed by a map to a nonzero ring. -/
theorem mem_supp_pullback_iff_of_exists_span_eq_ker {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (g : X ⟶ Y)
    [IsPreimmersion g] (F : Y.Modules) [F.IsFiniteType] (x : X)
    (ht : ∃ t : Y.presheaf.stalk (g x), RingHom.ker (g.stalkMap x).hom = Ideal.span {t}) :
    x ∈ SheafOfModules.supp ((Scheme.Modules.pullback g).obj F) ↔
      g x ∈ SheafOfModules.supp F := by
  obtain ⟨t, hspan⟩ := ht
  have hfin : Module.Finite (Y.presheaf.stalk (g x)) (F.presheaf.stalk (g x)) :=
    SheafOfModules.finite_stalk Y.sheaf F (g x)
  have key : Nontrivial (((Scheme.Modules.pullback g).obj F).presheaf.stalk x) ↔
      Nontrivial (F.presheaf.stalk (g x)) := by
    rw [← Module.length_pos_iff (R := X.presheaf.stalk x),
      length_stalk_pullback_eq_length_quotSMulTop g F x t hspan, Module.length_pos_iff]
    exact nontrivial_quotSMulTop_iff (mem_maximalIdeal_of_span_eq_ker_stalkMap g x t hspan)
  exact (SheafOfModules.mem_supp_iff_nontrivial_stalk ((Scheme.Modules.pullback g).obj F) x).trans
    (key.trans (SheafOfModules.mem_supp_iff_nontrivial_stalk F (g x)).symm)

variable (K : Type u) [Field K]

/-! ### The coherent sheaf of the counterexample -/

/-- The coherent sheaf on `𝐏¹_K` carried by the image of the zero section: the direct image of
the structure sheaf of `Spec K` along that section, which is a closed immersion by
`Stacks.Chow.isClosedImmersion_zeroSection`. -/
def fieldZeroSectionSheaf (K : Type u) [Field K] :
    (projectiveLineProduct (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S)).Modules :=
  (Scheme.Modules.pushforward (zeroSection (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S))).obj
    (Ample.unitModule (fieldChowSituation K).S)

/-- The family of projective lines over `Spec K` is locally Noetherian: it is of finite type over
`Spec K`, which is locally Noetherian as the base of a Chow situation. -/
instance isLocallyNoetherian_projectiveLineProduct_fieldChowSituation :
    IsLocallyNoetherian (projectiveLineProduct (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S)) :=
  LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian
    (pullback.fst (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S)
      (relativeProjectiveLine (fieldChowSituation K).S ↘ (fieldChowSituation K).S))

/-- The sheaf of the counterexample is coherent: it is the direct image of a structure sheaf
along a closed immersion into a locally Noetherian scheme. -/
instance isCoherent_fieldZeroSectionSheaf : (fieldZeroSectionSheaf K).IsCoherent :=
  isCoherent_pushforwardStructureSheaf _

/-- The zero fibre of the sheaf of the counterexample is coherent, so its cycle is defined. -/
instance isCoherent_zeroFibreModule_fieldZeroSectionSheaf :
    (zeroFibreModule (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S) (fieldZeroSectionSheaf K)).IsCoherent :=
  isCoherent_zeroFibreModule (fieldChowSituation K) (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S)
    (fieldZeroSectionSheaf K)

/-- The infinity fibre of the sheaf of the counterexample is coherent, so its cycle is
defined. -/
instance isCoherent_infinityFibreModule_fieldZeroSectionSheaf :
    (infinityFibreModule (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S) (fieldZeroSectionSheaf K)).IsCoherent :=
  isCoherent_infinityFibreModule (fieldChowSituation K) (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S)
    (fieldZeroSectionSheaf K)

/-- **The support of the sheaf of the counterexample is the image of the zero section.** Off the
image of a closed immersion the stalk of a direct image vanishes, and on the image it is a local
ring. -/
theorem supp_fieldZeroSectionSheaf :
    SheafOfModules.supp (fieldZeroSectionSheaf K) =
      Set.range (zeroSection (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S)) :=
  supp_pushforwardStructureSheaf _

/-- The zero section is a section of the structure morphism of the family of projective lines. -/
theorem zeroSection_comp_productBase_fieldChowSituation :
    zeroSection (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S) ≫
        pullback.fst (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S)
          (relativeProjectiveLine (fieldChowSituation K).S ↘ (fieldChowSituation K).S) ≫
          𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S =
      𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S := by
  rw [← Category.assoc, zeroSection_comp_fst, Category.id_comp]

/-- **Hypothesis (1) of Stacks 02S6 holds for the counterexample.** Every point of the support of
the sheaf lies on the zero section, where the relative dimension along the structure morphism of
the family is the relative dimension along the identity of `Spec K`, namely `0`. -/
theorem relativeDimension_le_of_mem_supp_fieldZeroSectionSheaf
    (ξ : projectiveLineProduct (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S))
    (hξ : ξ ∈ SheafOfModules.supp (fieldZeroSectionSheaf K)) :
    relativeDimension (fieldChowSituation K).dimensionFunction
      (productBase (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S)) ξ ≤ 0 + 1 := by
  rw [supp_fieldZeroSectionSheaf K] at hξ
  obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := hξ
  rw [relativeDimension_apply_of_section (fieldChowSituation K) (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S)
      (zeroSection (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S))
      (zeroSection_comp_productBase_fieldChowSituation K) y,
    relativeDimension_id_fieldChowSituation_eq_zero K y]
  omega

/-- **Hypothesis (3) of Stacks 02S6, read at the embedded associated points, holds vacuously for
the counterexample.** The support of the sheaf is the image of the zero section, which is a
single point because `Spec K` is; an associated point lies in the support, so the sheaf has no
two distinct associated points and hence no embedded associated point at all. -/
theorem not_isEmbeddedAssociatedPoint_fieldZeroSectionSheaf
    (ξ : projectiveLineProduct (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S)) :
    ¬ AlgebraicGeometry.IsEmbeddedAssociatedPoint (fieldZeroSectionSheaf K) ξ := by
  rintro ⟨hξ, ξ', hξ', -, hne⟩
  have hmem : ∀ η : projectiveLineProduct (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S),
      Stacks.Divisors.IsAssociatedPoint (fieldZeroSectionSheaf K) η →
      η ∈ Set.range (zeroSection (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S)) := fun η hη => by
    rw [← supp_fieldZeroSectionSheaf K]
    exact (SheafOfModules.mem_supp_iff_nontrivial_stalk _ η).mpr hη.nontrivial
  obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := hmem ξ hξ
  obtain ⟨y', rfl⟩ := hmem ξ' hξ'
  exact hne (congrArg _ (Subsingleton.elim y' y))

/-! ### The two fibre cycles -/

/-- The pullback of the sheaf of the counterexample along a locally principal preimmersion is
supported at the points mapping into the image of the zero section. -/
private theorem mem_supp_pullback_fieldZeroSectionSheaf_iff {X : Scheme.{u}}
    (g : X ⟶ projectiveLineProduct (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S)) [IsPreimmersion g] (x : X)
    (ht : ∃ t : _, RingHom.ker (g.stalkMap x).hom = Ideal.span {t}) :
    x ∈ SheafOfModules.supp ((Scheme.Modules.pullback g).obj (fieldZeroSectionSheaf K)) ↔
      g x ∈ Set.range (zeroSection (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S)) := by
  have _ : (fieldZeroSectionSheaf K).IsFiniteType :=
    isFiniteType_of_isCoherent (fieldZeroSectionSheaf K)
  rw [mem_supp_pullback_iff_of_exists_span_eq_ker g _ x ht, supp_fieldZeroSectionSheaf K]

/-- **The infinity fibre of the sheaf of the counterexample is zero.** Its support is the
preimage under the infinity section of the support of the sheaf, which is the image of the zero
section; the two sections have disjoint images. -/
theorem notMem_supp_infinityFibreModule_fieldZeroSectionSheaf (y : (fieldChowSituation K).S) :
    y ∉ SheafOfModules.supp
      (infinityFibreModule (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S) (fieldZeroSectionSheaf K)) := by
  rw [mem_supp_pullback_fieldZeroSectionSheaf_iff K (infinitySection (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S))
    y (exists_span_eq_ker_stalkMap_infinitySection (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S) y)]
  exact Set.disjoint_right.mp
    (disjoint_range_zeroSection_infinitySection (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S)) ⟨y, rfl⟩

/-- **The `0`-cycle of the infinity fibre vanishes**, that fibre being the zero sheaf. -/
theorem cycleAssociatedToCoherentSheaf_infinityFibreModule_fieldZeroSectionSheaf_eq_zero
    (hInf : schemeDeltaDimension (fieldChowSituation K)
      ((reducedSupport (infinityFibreModule (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S)
        (fieldZeroSectionSheaf K))).subschemeι ≫ 𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S)
        ≤ ((0 : ℤ) : EInt)) :
    cycleAssociatedToCoherentSheaf (fieldChowSituation K) (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S)
      (infinityFibreModule (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S) (fieldZeroSectionSheaf K)) 0 hInf = 0 := by
  classical
  refine Subtype.ext (Function.locallyFinsuppWithin.ext fun y => ?_)
  rw [cycleAssociatedToCoherentSheaf_apply (fieldChowSituation K) (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S)
    (infinityFibreModule (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S) (fieldZeroSectionSheaf K)) 0 hInf y,
    ite_eq_right fun h => notMem_supp_infinityFibreModule_fieldZeroSectionSheaf K y h.1]
  rfl

/-- **The `0`-cycle of the zero fibre does not vanish.** The support of the zero fibre is the
whole of `Spec K`, whose unique point has relative dimension `0`, so the coefficient there is the
length of the stalk of the zero fibre; that length is finite and nonzero. -/
theorem cycleAssociatedToCoherentSheaf_zeroFibreModule_fieldZeroSectionSheaf_ne_zero
    (h₀ : schemeDeltaDimension (fieldChowSituation K)
      ((reducedSupport (zeroFibreModule (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S)
        (fieldZeroSectionSheaf K))).subschemeι ≫ 𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S)
        ≤ ((0 : ℤ) : EInt)) :
    cycleAssociatedToCoherentSheaf (fieldChowSituation K) (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S)
      (zeroFibreModule (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S) (fieldZeroSectionSheaf K)) 0 h₀ ≠ 0 := by
  obtain ⟨x⟩ := nonempty_fieldChowSituation_base K
  have hx : relativeDimension (fieldChowSituation K).dimensionFunction
      (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S) x = 0 := relativeDimension_id_fieldChowSituation_eq_zero K x
  have hmem : x ∈ SheafOfModules.supp
      (zeroFibreModule (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S) (fieldZeroSectionSheaf K)) := by
    rw [mem_supp_pullback_fieldZeroSectionSheaf_iff K (zeroSection (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S)) x
      (exists_span_eq_ker_stalkMap_zeroSection (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S) x)]
    exact ⟨x, rfl⟩
  have hpos := sheafMultiplicity_pos_of_mem_supp
    (zeroFibreModule (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S) (fieldZeroSectionSheaf K))
    (isFiniteLength_stalk_of_relativeDimension_eq (fieldChowSituation K)
      (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S)
      (zeroFibreModule (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S) (fieldZeroSectionSheaf K)) h₀ hx) hmem
  intro hzero
  have hcoeff := cycleAssociatedToCoherentSheaf_apply_of_relativeDimension_eq
    (fieldChowSituation K) (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S)
    (zeroFibreModule (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S) (fieldZeroSectionSheaf K)) 0 h₀ hx
  rw [hzero] at hcoeff
  have h0 : sheafMultiplicity
      (zeroFibreModule (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S) (fieldZeroSectionSheaf K)) x = 0 := by
    rw [← hcoeff]
    rfl
  exact hpos.ne' h0

/-! ### The refutation -/

/-- **Stacks 02S6 is false with hypothesis (3) read at the embedded associated points, as the
source states it.** There is no implication from

1. every point of `Supp(F)` has relative dimension at most `k + 1`,
2. `dim_δ(Supp(F₀)) ≤ k` and `dim_δ(Supp(F_∞)) ≤ k`,
3. every embedded associated point of `F` either misses both distinguished sections or has
   relative dimension below `k`,

to `[F₀]_k ∼_rat [F_∞]_k`.

The witness is the Chow situation over a field with `X = S = Spec K`, `f = 𝟙`, `k = 0` and
`F = Stacks.Chow.fieldZeroSectionSheaf K` the structure sheaf of the image of the zero section.
All three hypotheses hold — (1) by
`Stacks.Chow.relativeDimension_le_of_mem_supp_fieldZeroSectionSheaf`, (2) because every closed
subscheme of `Spec K` has delta-dimension `0`, and (3) vacuously, by
`Stacks.Chow.not_isEmbeddedAssociatedPoint_fieldZeroSectionSheaf` — while `[F₀]₀ ≠ 0 = [F_∞]₀`
and no two distinct `0`-cycles on `Spec K` are rationally equivalent, by
`Stacks.Chow.eq_of_rationallyEquivalent_fieldChowSituation`.

The statement refuted is
`Stacks.Chow.rationallyEquivalent_cycleAssociatedToCoherentSheaf_fibres` with its hypothesis (3)
restricted to the embedded associated points; with (3) at every associated point, as there, the
instance fails (3). -/
theorem not_forall_rationallyEquivalent_of_isEmbeddedAssociatedPoint :
    ¬ ∀ (C : ChowSituation.{u}) (X : Scheme.{u}) (f : X ⟶ C.S) [LocallyOfFiniteType f] (k : ℤ)
        (F : (projectiveLineProduct f).Modules) [F.IsCoherent],
      schemeDeltaDimension C ((reducedSupport F).subschemeι ≫ productBase f) ≤
          ((k + 1 : ℤ) : EInt) →
      ∀ (h₀ : haveI := isCoherent_zeroFibreModule C f F
          schemeDeltaDimension C ((reducedSupport (zeroFibreModule f F)).subschemeι ≫ f) ≤
            (k : EInt))
        (hInf : haveI := isCoherent_infinityFibreModule C f F
          schemeDeltaDimension C ((reducedSupport (infinityFibreModule f F)).subschemeι ≫ f) ≤
            (k : EInt)),
      (∀ ξ : projectiveLineProduct f, AlgebraicGeometry.IsEmbeddedAssociatedPoint F ξ →
        ξ ∉ Set.range (zeroSection f) ∪ Set.range (infinitySection f) ∨
          relativeDimension C.dimensionFunction (productBase f) ξ < k) →
      haveI := isCoherent_zeroFibreModule C f F
      haveI := isCoherent_infinityFibreModule C f F
      RationallyEquivalent C f k
        (cycleAssociatedToCoherentSheaf C f (zeroFibreModule f F) k h₀)
        (cycleAssociatedToCoherentSheaf C f (infinityFibreModule f F) k hInf) := by
  intro h
  let Q := ULift.{u} ℚ
  have hSupp : schemeDeltaDimension (fieldChowSituation Q)
      ((reducedSupport (fieldZeroSectionSheaf Q)).subschemeι ≫
        productBase (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation Q).S)) ≤ (((0 : ℤ) + 1 : ℤ) : EInt) :=
    schemeDeltaDimension_le_of_forall_relativeDimension_le _ _ _ fun w => by
      refine relativeDimension_le_of_mem_supp_fieldZeroSectionSheaf Q _ ?_
      have hw : (reducedSupport (fieldZeroSectionSheaf Q)).subschemeι w ∈
          Set.range (reducedSupport (fieldZeroSectionSheaf Q)).subschemeι := ⟨w, rfl⟩
      rwa [Scheme.IdealSheafData.range_subschemeι, coe_support_reducedSupport] at hw
  refine cycleAssociatedToCoherentSheaf_zeroFibreModule_fieldZeroSectionSheaf_ne_zero Q
    (schemeDeltaDimension_le_zero_fieldChowSituation Q _) ?_
  refine (eq_of_rationallyEquivalent_fieldChowSituation Q _ _
    (h (fieldChowSituation Q) _ (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation Q).S) 0 (fieldZeroSectionSheaf Q)
      hSupp (schemeDeltaDimension_le_zero_fieldChowSituation Q _)
      (schemeDeltaDimension_le_zero_fieldChowSituation Q _)
      fun ξ hξ => absurd hξ (not_isEmbeddedAssociatedPoint_fieldZeroSectionSheaf Q ξ))).trans ?_
  exact cycleAssociatedToCoherentSheaf_infinityFibreModule_fieldZeroSectionSheaf_eq_zero Q _

end Stacks.Chow

end
